            <ArticleTitle>[Progabide treatment of a case of the syndrome of painful legs and moving toes].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>422-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is presently no recognised therapy for the painful legs and moving toes syndrome. Treatment by progabide, a GABA-agonist, was successful in one case: a gradual improvement was observed during four weeks and the movements have now disappeared after six months of progabide therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
